# (build 112) The AUDIO page's TAILS: FADE ends a note struck again in 15 ms, as the chip's one note a
# channel (the default, 111b's); RING lets it ring out its own release on a
# voice of its own (111a's)
# (docs/audio.md, "Build 112"). It is Q's: route_probe is built without Q
# and the chip plays, so the line under it says Q ONLY and the title's theme
# plays on through every change. Two values: left, right and C each flip it.
# The route reads its own settings.json, never the player's.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
expect audio tails FADE / Q ONLY
press right
expect audio tails RING / Q ONLY
wait ticks 10
shot page_tails_ring
expect sound playing
press left
expect audio tails FADE / Q ONLY
press c
expect audio tails RING / Q ONLY
press c
expect audio tails FADE / Q ONLY
wait ticks 12
expect sound playing
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
